@GavinSBaker Her proposed policies are very reasonable and in line with how responsible operators have been operating in the state for years. 

Also important to remember that TCEQ permitting likely reopens in December for a month or so before she takes office. I strongly suspect folks currently lacking permits but planning to deliver 2028 data center capacity will be able to get approved for construction during this window. And in any event, I think both parties in TX are on-board with her position, so more comprehensive legislation (which also reopens the TCEQ permitting process) will likely come months, not years after she takes office.

IMO net impact is that some of the ill-prepared, disorganized, more speculative projects get started ~6-9 months later than planned (or cancelled outright).. But folks intimate with the TX regulatory processes with years of experience building in TX could end up largely unaffected.
